# Line endings that survive a Windows checkout.
#
# GitHub's Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf=true, which would give
# the shell scripts CRLF endings; bash then reads the trailing CR as part of
# the command and the CI job fails before it runs a single check. These files
# are executed by a shell, so they keep LF everywhere.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
